Empty streets and local voices can be found in neighborhoods a few blocks away from busy areas in Venice.
Piazza San Marco is a waterfront square in Venice.
Piazza San Marco includes the Basilica, cafes beneath porticoes, and the Campanile.
High tide occasionally causes water to slosh around in Piazza San Marco.
The Basilica di San Marco is a Byzantine basilica.
The Basilica di San Marco glitters with golden mosaics inside.
