The Cathédrale Saint-Nicolas has five tiled onion domes.
The Cathédrale Saint-Nicolas is considered one of the most important Russian Orthodox buildings outside the Russian Federation.
The interior of the Cathédrale Saint-Nicolas is filled with blue floral patterns and icons in gilded frames.
The Cours Saleya in the Old Town is a well-trodden tourist spot.
